{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unangry-fernlike-koala","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nusage-log rows (src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py) record the four token fields but not model, provider, or timestamp, and the plan-review budget shedder prices work with hard-coded guesses (COST_SINGLE_TURN_USD=0.006, COST_AGENT_USD=0.12, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:107-109). No provider publishes a machine-readable price API; pydantic's genai-prices package bundles offline price data with cache read/write tiers, historical prices by timestamp, and a typed LookupError for unknown models — and pydantic-ai's RequestUsage already implements its AbstractUsage protocol. Operator approved it as an optional add-in with graceful fallback.\n\n## Approach\n(1) Extend each usage-log row with model, inferred provider (the mapping at src/rebar/llm/config.py:321-327 already computes it), and a UTC ISO timestamp — all in hand at record() time. (2) In `python -m rebar.llm.usage_log summarize`, attempt `import genai_prices`; when importable, compute per-row cost via calc_price with the row timestamp, catching LookupError per row so unknown models/providers (including the fake test runner) yield cost None and the summary reports \"excludes N unpriced calls\"; when not importable, print token totals with the cost column reading \"unavailable (install rebar[pricing])\". (3) Declare a new optional extra `pricing = [\"genai-prices\"]` in pyproject.toml. Never a hard error, never a silently-wrong number; the summary column is labeled \"est. cost\". Alternative rejected: vendoring LiteLLM's ~2 MB price JSON — takes on key-normalization and schema-drift ownership that genai-prices maintains upstream.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/usage_log.py, pyproject.toml, tests/llm/test_usage_log_pricing.py, docs/llm-framework.md (usage-log section).\n\n## Testing\nUnit: rows gain the three new fields; summarize with genai_prices stubbed prices known rows, marks unknown rows unpriced, and totals annotate the exclusion; summarize with the import failing prints the unavailable message and exits 0; old-format rows without the new fields still summarize.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] New usage-log rows carry model, provider, and UTC timestamp (checked: unit test on record()).\n- [ ] With genai-prices installed, summarize prints per-model est. cost and marks unknown models as unpriced without raising (checked: unit test with a stubbed price module and a fake-runner row).\n- [ ] Without genai-prices, summarize prints token totals and \"unavailable (install rebar[pricing])\" and exits 0 (checked: unit test with import blocked).\n- [ ] Rows written by the previous format still summarize without error (checked: fixture test).","id":"41be-a71e-3074-4e7d","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Optional genai-prices cost accounting in usage-log summarize"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384358962766001,"uuid":"a4c22b6c-397f-4718-aaaa-73d7f3c46337"}